Evidence for ToyOSOrg/ToyOS#976 (scheduler stage 2: topology and roster).

Home and source paths are written <src>, <dev>, <scratch>, <session> and
$TMPDIR; nothing else is changed or dropped. Revisions are ToyOS commits on
branch wt/toyos-topology-2, base d5713917d (#974).

host/
  ci-host.log                `cargo run -- --ci host` at dce097b4b: EXIT=0, 88 of 88 green.
  ci-host-cap-lift-red.log   the same at b34e6fb63: EXIT=1, clippy red (len_without_is_empty,
                             chunks_exact_to_as_chunks); fixed in dce097b4b.
  ci-host-part1-red.log      the same at f51c3b45e (part 1 before amend): EXIT=1, the new PPTT
                             fixture undeclared in build/licence.rs; fixed in 4ee067034.
  build-lib-part1.log        `cargo test --lib` (the build system's step) at 4ee067034: EXIT=0.

guest/
  guest.log                  `cargo test --test toyos-build -- desktop_without_x2apic virt_smp
                             virt_failed_ap_leaves_no_hole` at dce097b4b: EXIT=0, 3 of 3.
  guest-virt-part1.log       `... -- virt_failed_ap_leaves_no_hole virt_smp` at 4ee067034: EXIT=0.
  guest-x86-part1.log        `... -- desktop_without_x2apic` at 4ee067034: EXIT=0.

boots/  manual `cargo run -- [--arch aarch64] --smp N --console-boot`, stopped by hand once
        `Boot: complete` was read
  x86-tcg-16-red.log, -blackbox.txt, -registers.txt
                             on the uncommitted tree before b34e6fb63, whose trace table was
                             one allocation: the kernel
                             printed nothing; QMP `info registers -a` put CPU0 in
                             `hold_the_panel` with every AP in firmware, and the black box page
                             (`pmemsave 0x8000000`) says `GlobalAlloc: 4195328 bytes exceeds
                             MAX_HEAP_ALLOC (2093056)`.
  x86-tcg-16.log             the tree committed as b34e6fb63: SMP 16 of 16, 15 APs join.
  aarch64-hvf-12.log         the same tree: SMP 12 of 12 through the PPTT.
  x86-tcg-4-part1.log, aarch64-hvf-4-part1.log
                             part 1 before commit: the first `topo:` lines on each architecture.

controls/
  controls.log + m1..m5 patches   against f51c3b45e (part 1); each applied with `git apply`,
                             its test run, the patch reverted: all EXIT=101, each red on the
                             claim it mutates. None of the files they touch changed after.
  controls-2.log + m6, m7    against dce097b4b: EXIT=101 each.

metal-staging/
  stage-t14.log, stage-amd.log, request-*.txt
                             `cargo test --test toyos-build -- --metal --metal-readback <dir>
                             topology_readback smp_roster_and_tsc_trail trace_read counters_read
                             inbox_log_post disk_backtrace` at dce097b4b: EXIT=2 (staged, one boot
                             each, no machine touched).

pptt/
  find_table.py, dump_pptt.py, dump.txt
                             scratch tools that found the PPTT in the `pmemsave` of QEMU 11.1.1
                             `virt`'s RAM (lib/acpi/fixtures/qemu-11.1.1-virt-pptt/SOURCE) and
                             decoded its structures by hand from ACPI 6.5 §5.2.30, apart from
                             the decoder under test.

metal/  (appended for f91f2601a)
  rejudge-amd.log, rejudge-t14.log
                             the orchestrator's readbacks of dce097b4b's staged images,
                             re-judged with no machine touched by `cargo test --test
                             toyos-build -- --metal --metal-readback <dir> topology_readback
                             smp_roster_and_tsc_trail trace_read counters_read inbox_log_post
                             disk_backtrace` at dce097b4b plus the row fix committed as
                             f91f2601a: EXIT=0 on each, AMD `SMP: 16 of 16`, 8 cores in 2
                             LLCs. Under dce097b4b's own row the AMD judge failed only on its
                             x2APIC expectation; the bench's CPUs report CPUID.01H:ECX[21]
                             clear (scout word 0x76d8320b), so the row's claim was the T14's.

r1/  (review round 1 fixes; branch rebased onto b48aab819, #973)
  ci-host.log                `cargo run -- --ci host` at 767c1469f: EXIT=0, 88 of 88 green.
  guest.log                  `cargo test --test toyos-build -- desktop_without_x2apic virt_smp
                             virt_failed_ap_leaves_no_hole` at 767c1469f: EXIT=0, 3 of 3.
  controls-3.log + m8, m9    against 36000e3fb (767c1469f before the rebase, same tree but for
                             main's #973): m8 stores the length before the claim and
                             `kernel-loom`'s `cpu_slice` test reds; m9 counts only caches whose
                             type is declared valid and `a_cache_of_undeclared_type_still_places_
                             its_node` reds. EXIT=101 each.
  The PPTT refusal's citation was read in Arm BBR 2.2 (DEN0044I, the PDF Arm's documentation
  service serves for den0044/latest, sha256 0cfb946c12fcd91e4e0d19b82090856fabb6b0141d6439e86c42974431625377):
  §3.1 puts sections 4-8 on systems using the SBBR recipe; §7.3.1 "Mandatory ACPI tables ...
  mandatory for all compliant systems" lists §7.3.1.10 PPTT.
